From c179bcae3123bb5864ae81858eda9eecd5c6d32f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:46:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: a node construction passes over is built afresh

Construction builds no box for some nodes: an inline that its inline
root's layout takes in, a table's row, a child of a table that is not a
cell. It spent their construction damage and kept what they had built
as boxes: their layout children, and those children's own. Nothing
builds them while they are passed over, and the damage a delta leaves
under them is cleared with the rest, so the lists went on naming the
nodes it freed, and none it added. When such a node was a box again
(its table's display removed, say), resolve found no damage on it and
kept them: Taffy laid out a freed node ("invalid SlotMap key used" at
node_from_id), and paint read one from a stale paint list. In debug
builds, assert_layout_parents_consistent failed as soon as an inline was
taken into its parent's inline layout.

A node construction passes over now forgets its layout children, and
theirs down the boxes it owned, each flagged PASSED_OVER. A flagged
node that is a layout child again is built afresh with its subtree:
damaged, its layout caches cleared, as a new subtree is. Constructing a
node clears the flag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
